# Normalise the scripts that have to survive a round trip through a filesystem
# that does not agree with us about line endings.
#
# A shell script stored with CRLF endings fails on Linux and macOS with
# "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory", which is
# a confusing way to find out your editor defaulted to Windows endings. Pin it.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
